  "draw": "census: all 95 witnesses of census.json, in order",
  "transcript": "Canonical serialization rule: take the proposal artifact exactly as given, serialize it as JSON with sorted keys and no whitespace, persist the exact bytes as proposal_canon.json, then compute hProposal = SHA-256(proposal_canon.json) and seed = SHA-256(hProposal + salt). A third party can re-derive by hashing the same proposal_canon.json bytes to reproduce hProposal, then hashing (hProposal || salt) to reproduce seedHex; mechanical check: sha256sum proposal_canon.json must equal hProposal, and sha256sum of the concatenation (hProposal + salt) must equal seedHex. (Recursive sorted keys, no whitespace; transcript describes the hashing steps, not the candidate.)"
